<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ watchdog to probe Fletcher, ECNZ stakes in Kupe.</title>
<headline>NZ watchdog to probe Fletcher, ECNZ stakes in Kupe.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's anti-trust Commerce Commission said on Thursday it was investigating Fletcher Energy increasing its stake in the Kupe gas field and state power generator Electricity Corp taking a stake in the field.  </p>
<p>The commission noted Fletcher had extensive interests in natural gas markets through a range of companies.</p>
<p>Bollard said the investigation would take a few weeks.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
